# Two alternatives on one line each carry `X "("`; NUM's decides nothing
# (nothing after NUM shifts "("). A used hint on a sibling alternative of
# the same line does not hide it: hints group by alternative, not by line.
# error: x_hint_dead_beside_used.grammar:21:
# error: X "(" on expr → NUM has no effect
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    num
    lparen
    rparen
    eof
    err
'('                                         → lparen
')'                                         → rparen
[a-z]+                                      → ident
[0-9]+                                      → num
.                                           → err
@parser
exprs! = expr+                              → (exprs ...1)
expr   = IDENT X "(" | NUM X "("
       | IDENT "(" expr ")"                 → (call 1 3)
       | "(" expr ")"                       → 2
